Cell[TextData[{
 "\nThe Leggett-Garg ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["K", "TI"], "2"], "(", 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], ")"}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "K_2(t)", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "58b44fc0-5cb5-044b-a5c2-20b8c10b4a1e"],
 " has been shown above to not obey the inequality ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["K", "TI"], "2"], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           StyleBox["t", "TI"], ")"}], "\[LessEqual]", "1"}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "K_2(t) \\leq 1", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9e86312e-9d3d-cc49-b19e-6f9777257c11"],
 " which indicates that the spin-1/2 system is properly quantum and does not \
evolve macro-realistically."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998590966378208*^9, 3.9985910635117416`*^9}, {
   3.9985917172666435`*^9, 3.9985917681957073`*^9}, 
   3.9985918389834213`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"d6dc488d-4977-ad46-a75b-\
cb4fa3102f1a"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Spin-1", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9985917960529423`*^9, 
  3.9985918035081444`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"87261f1f-ec11-1846-bebf-\
b92516133437"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The spin-1 system is the natural extension of the canonical spin-1/2 \
example to a three-level system, i.e. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], "\[Element]", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"-1", ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "q \\in \\{-1, 0 , 1\\}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "07a7f644-d299-344e-a899-1c9966b5f7db"],
 ". However, as we will show, the three-level operator is already \
sufficiently different from the two-level operator that even for the simplest \
example of a spin-1 in a magnetic field, the traditional Leggett-Garg \
inequality is always satisfied. \n\nLeggett-Garg tests for n-level systems \
are typically dealt with in three ways:\n\n1) Using the weak measure \
technique which provides a valid quantum correlation function for any n-level \
system.\n\n2) The projector operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "\[CapitalPi]S\[Theta]nLevel"], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "750eb012-5904-1246-b57f-600654bfd0e9"],
 " can be easily fitted to be a 2-level operator with eigenvalues ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], "\[Element]", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"-1", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "q\\in\\{-1,1\\}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0008be04-6edb-3449-ba95-750e623a5f33"],
 ". This latter method is more popular in the literature and can be used to \
increase the value of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["K", "TI"], "(", 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], ")"}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "K(t)", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cf15e283-9436-244a-a95f-cf6786c4e55b"],
 " past the maximum allowed for a 2-level system ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
            RowBox[{
              StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
              StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
              StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], 
           RowBox[{"(", 
             StyleBox["t", "TI"], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
           FractionBox["3", "2"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "(K_{max}(t) = \\frac{3}{2})", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8b64842e-4787-744a-8518-f5512a5f88e1"],
 ".\n\n3) We can use the same test with the traditionally defined ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["q", "TI"]], "(", 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], ")"}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "C_q(t)", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "41aae4d0-af4c-df45-aa40-d078dd31611c"],
 " time correlation function, ignoring that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["Q", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "Q", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "53e7e0a1-5160-0445-96e0-e90e8a3025eb"],
 " is a trichotomic/3-level operator. This works specifically because the \
expression ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "+", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "q_iq_j + q_jq_k - q_iq_k", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0fc6f3dc-ce43-c94e-bbd4-b402f8d53a67"],
 " is still less than or equal to 1 for all values of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], "\[Element]", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"-1", ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "q \\in \\{-1, 0, 1\\}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4d4d9f0b-342d-6043-a78a-c5c7edfcaf21"],
 ". Even though the Leggett-Garg inequality is always satisfied for the \
spin-1 example, other three-level systems do exist which violate the \
Legget-Garg inequality. \n\nHowever, there is a fourth option which I have \
not seen explored in the literature which is to go back to the original LG \
bound and modify it for the additional possibility that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["q", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "q", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "372faf2b-fa4c-cb4e-b653-e57651d2e6fd"],
 " can now take the value of 0. For example,"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998591816847313*^9, 3.998591915882496*^9}, 
   3.9985919469680996`*^9, {3.9985920189782524`*^9, 3.998592100120985*^9}, {
   3.9985921343362503`*^9, 3.998592173343912*^9}, {3.99859223075918*^9, 
   3.998592387828108*^9}, {3.998592451420471*^9, 3.9985924620426846`*^9}, {
   3.998592528889475*^9, 3.9985926680274773`*^9}, {3.9985927125354176`*^9, 
   3.998592778139824*^9}, {3.99859284786154*^9, 3.9985928987165756`*^9}, {
   3.998592938275076*^9, 3.9985929953403015`*^9}, {3.9985931070348873`*^9, 
   3.9985931124016666`*^9}, {3.9985990783369446`*^9, 3.998599101186159*^9}, {
   3.9985994927626095`*^9, 3.9985995005685616`*^9}, {3.998599552757433*^9, 
   3.9985996041307964`*^9}, {3.9985996519971714`*^9, 3.998599934096388*^9}, {
   3.998652467252939*^9, 3.9986524943209496`*^9}, {3.9986525675931396`*^9, 
   3.9986527307421303`*^9}, {3.9986527986815643`*^9, 
   3.9986528378049183`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1c1ba7e7-e6b5-dd44-bc5e-\
379290d47a0c"],

Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
      RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "+", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[LessEqual]", "|", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "+", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "|", "-", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
    "q_iq_j + q_jq_k - q_i q_k \\leq |q_i + q_k | - q_iq_k", "state" -> 
    "Boxes"|>,
   "TeXAssistantTemplate"], 
  TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"e14d40af-2cc1-e844-978d-fa9b79e93723"]], \
"Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.998652850299658*^9},
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"64fa5cb0-2218-7c4a-b277-71c3a9583d8c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As mentioned before, this inequality is still valid for three-level \
systems, however the right hand side is not equal to 1, as it was for 2-level \
operators. However, for all combinations of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["i", "TI"]], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "(q_i, q_k)", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5c20223c-4a10-1648-8982-f781ba5e2789"],
 ", the right hand side is only not equal to 1 when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "q_i = q_j = 0", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0b6f6c68-543d-7d4b-ae9d-5b914cf47fb1"],
 ", in which case the right hand side is zero. Therefore,"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998652878888918*^9, 
  3.9986530945904274`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8850ad28-5ff5-8f47-a7b5-\
daf92848b302"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"|", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "+", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "|", "-", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "1", "-", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"1", "-", 
             SubsuperscriptBox[
              StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
              StyleBox["i", "TI"], "2"]}], ")"}], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"1", "-", 
             SubsuperscriptBox[
              StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
              StyleBox["k", "TI"], "2"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "|q_i + q_k | - q_iq_k  =  1 - (1 - q_i^2)(1- q_k^2)", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "54486cbc-2058-f04c-940c-963d81639e9c"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998653100479765*^9, 3.998653112138891*^9}, 
   3.9986532262062683`*^9},
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"30e77259-b6e5-f24b-8682-d24ec2e296b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Where the equality is point-wise for the three allowed values of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], "."}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "q.", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b63ee406-f37f-dc47-8c33-1d8085d34a3a"],
 " Substituting this in for the inequality and expanding the right hand side \
gives an inequality which is easily verifiable."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9986532182626457`*^9, 3.998653324488882*^9}, {
  3.9986534347299004`*^9, 
  3.9986535250274982`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"31d81837-2a58-f54e-98fc-\
0452b10aeeac"],

Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
      RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "+", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[LessEqual]", 
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["i", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["k", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
    "q_iq_j + q_jq_k - q_i q_k \\leq q_i^2 +q_k^2 - q_iq_k", "state" -> 
    "Boxes"|>,
   "TeXAssistantTemplate"], 
  TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"b0309b0b-d2dd-184b-936b-09e1919d9c2c"]], \
"Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.998653539872568*^9},
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"b1a9236f-f29c-684a-81e3-ec58f92a6ad6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Plugging this into the Leggett-Garg inequality, multiplying each side by \
the probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["j", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "p_{ijk}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "847ef1c0-e199-b941-b536-59673a28cf15"],
 ", and then summing over the possibilities gives the updated Leggett-Garg \
inequality for three-level systems."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9986532182626457`*^9, 3.998653324488882*^9}, {
  3.9986534347299004`*^9, 
  3.9986535187973423`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7da34759-baee-fb45-a7bc-\
ad24ed3e6b59"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"2", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["q", "TI"]], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           StyleBox["t", "TI"], ")"}], "-", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["q", "TI"]], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"2", 
             StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], ")"}], "\[LessEqual]", "1", "-", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{"1", "-", 
            SuperscriptBox[
             StyleBox["q", "TI"], "2"]}]], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"2", 
             StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {},
      "input" -> "2C_{q}(t) - C_q(2t) \\leq 1 - C_{1-q^2}(2t)", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "20dea0d8-0713-be48-8177-b51df74f8774"],
 "\nor\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["K", "TI"], "3"], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           StyleBox["t", "TI"], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", "2", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["q", "TI"]], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           StyleBox["t", "TI"], ")"}], "-", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["q", "TI"]], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"2", 
             StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], ")"}], "+", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{"1", "-", 
            SuperscriptBox[
             StyleBox["q", "TI"], "2"]}]], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"2", 
             StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], ")"}], "\[LessEqual]", "1"}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "K_3(t) = 2C_{q}(t) - C_q(2t) + C_{1- q^2}(2t) \\leq  1", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c72b0083-c978-1b4f-8997-a46bbe602f8c"]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9986533774225693`*^9, 3.998653380263666*^9}, {
  3.9986535795225143`*^9, 3.9986536089551964`*^9}},
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"eb1e8228-80db-0d40-9380-e0f0cb9d987e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This last equation is our updated Leggett-Garg inequality for the \
three-level system. Note that I have rearranged the equation above it to \
preserve the structure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["K", "TI"], "3"], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           StyleBox["t", "TI"], ")"}], "\[LessEqual]", "1"}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "K_3(t) \\leq 1", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f6c9212a-4cd7-b04e-9053-2d6bc7d76fb4"],
 ". Now, let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s look at how this updated inequality plays out \
in the spin-1 example compared to the original LG inequality."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9986536134091625`*^9, 3.9986536193729687`*^9}, {
  3.9986538033941727`*^9, 
  3.998653988082531*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3e1eb4b9-d87a-cb46-8e41-\
5ea9f63dc897"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Trichotomic LG bound", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9860671872079353`*^9, 3.9860671900712605`*^9}, {
  3.9986540152034035`*^9, 
  3.998654024018385*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e69876d6-7cc1-ac4f-b867-\
d7d36f079457"],

Cell["\<\
Our basis is now 3-dimensional corresponding to the three possible \
measurements of the spin of a spin-1 particle.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9986541540248833`*^9, 
  3.9986541845479336`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c6a1ad10-6e62-9f4b-8ed1-\
48390bfecc30"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"splus", "=", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"s0", "=", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "1", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sminus", "=", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"StateVec", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"splus", ",", " ", "s0", ",", " ", "sminus"}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"rho", "[", 
    RowBox[{"H_", ",", "\[Beta]_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"1", "/", 
     RowBox[{"Z", "[", "\[Beta]", "]"}]}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
        RowBox[{"S", ",", "S"}], "]"}], "*", 
       RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "\[Beta]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"S", ".", "H", ".", "S"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"S", ",", "StateVec"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998654199298582*^9, 3.9986542161699734`*^9}, {
  3.9986555360875607`*^9, 3.998655537854738*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[285]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7af6c648-b700-714b-9c1e-b0c873645ca9"],

Cell["\<\
The spin operators of the spin-1 particle are now three-dimensional Hermitian \
matrices and are no longer unitary.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.99865405120648*^9, 3.9986540884050293`*^9}, {
  3.998654221986326*^9, 
  3.9986542309960136`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4362f824-7be3-e244-b090-\
a1b51db1266c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Sz", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", 
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Sx", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"1", "/", 
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", "1", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", "1", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Sy", " ", "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"1", "/", 
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", 
        RowBox[{"-", "I"}], ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"I", ",", "0", ",", 
        RowBox[{"-", "I"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", "I", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Id", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Svec", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"Sx", ",", "Sy", ",", "Sz"}], "}"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9860458882935677`*^9, 3.9860459045717716`*^9}, {
  3.9860459408328323`*^9, 3.9860459847471886`*^9}, {3.998654239539896*^9, 
  3.9986542604339848`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[290]:=",ExpressionUUID->"03063080-8ee7-654f-9e80-8d2708b9ddb0"],

Cell["\<\
As before, we will take the Hamiltonian to be of a magnetic field along the \
z-axis.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9986542769950066`*^9, 
  3.998654305428047*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2ca3a5d6-8247-5741-bbc4-\
d50b0432b164"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"H", " ", "=", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"-", "Sz"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"H", "//", "MatrixForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9860630848324337`*^9, 3.986063110231804*^9}, {
   3.9984042363786926`*^9, 3.99840424547003*^9}, {3.9984283713600483`*^9, 
   3.9984284677838326`*^9}, {3.998429704104658*^9, 3.9984297047674522`*^9}, 
   3.998654148368641*^9, 3.9986542352996426`*^9, {3.9986542735259666`*^9, 
   3.9986543090041313`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[257]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ab0e8b3f-3acb-2240-95a1-583c3c6ec01f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "0", "0"},
     {"0", "0", "0"},
     {"0", "0", "1"}
    },
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
         Offset[0.7]}, 
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
        Offset[0.2], {
         Offset[0.4]}, 
        Offset[0.2]}}], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}],
  Function[BoxForm`e$, 
   MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9986543094182873`*^9, 3.998654503567934*^9, 
  3.9986548203202286`*^9, 3.998655330789276*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[258]//MatrixForm=",ExpressionUUID->"ab2cebc5-aef1-b14c-8edb-\
d9cdcd88b3d0"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The projection operator for the three level system with eigenvalues {-1, 0, \
1} is more involved than the two level system, but it is analytically \
solvable.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9986545761423206`*^9, 
  3.998654630886116*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1b66c846-aa4d-0f43-8cf6-\
15ca0b71e828"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"S\[Theta]Spin1", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\[Theta]_", ",", "t_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Udag", "[", 
    RowBox[{"H", ",", "t"}], "]"}], ".", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "Sx"}], " ", "+", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "Sz"}]}], ")"}], ".", 
   RowBox[{"U", "[", 
    RowBox[{"H", ",", "t"}], "]"}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalPi]S\[Theta]3Level", "[", 
   RowBox[{"q_", ",", "t_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"q", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], "Id"}], " ", "+", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"q", " ", 
      RowBox[{"S\[Theta]Spin1", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", "t"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"3", "/", "2"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"q", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"S\[Theta]Spin1", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", "t"}], "]"}], ".", 
     RowBox[{"S\[Theta]Spin1", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", "t"}], "]"}]}]}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998654634653145*^9, 3.9986546347481823`*^9}, {
  3.9986546663591003`*^9, 3.998654706235964*^9}, {3.9986547420351143`*^9, 
  3.998654769493511*^9}, {3.99865504930777*^9, 3.998655166577038*^9}, {
  3.998655233823393*^9, 3.998655234155987*^9}, {3.9986558220117645`*^9, 
  3.9986558431782017`*^9}, {3.9986559241220245`*^9, 3.9986559266360207`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[304]:=",ExpressionUUID->"06ae6e50-0b9e-ca49-94fb-245332d112b3"],

Cell["\<\
We will also initialize a function which implements the strong measure \
formula since the strong and weak measure formulas no longer coincide.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998654331236862*^9, 
  3.9986543847119064`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"78953824-87ca-774b-bdea-\
9909a2731e4a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ThermalStateExpectation", "[", 
   RowBox[{"H_", ",", "\[Beta]_", ",", "op_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"rho", "[", 
     RowBox[{"H", ",", "\[Beta]"}], "]"}], ".", "op"}], "]"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"CqStrongMeasure", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\[Beta]_", ",", " ", "op_", ",", "t_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"q1", " ", "q2", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ThermalStateExpectation", "[", 
       RowBox[{"H", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"op", "[", 
          RowBox[{"q1", ",", "0"}], "]"}], ".", 
         RowBox[{"op", "[", 
          RowBox[{"q2", ",", "t"}], "]"}], ".", 
         RowBox[{"op", "[", 
          RowBox[{"q1", ",", "0"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"q1", ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"q2", ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
   "]"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"COneMinusQSquaredStrongMeasure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Beta]_", ",", " ", "op_", ",", "t_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", "-", 
         RowBox[{"q1", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"q2", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"ThermalStateExpectation", "[", 
        RowBox[{"H", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"op", "[", 
           RowBox[{"q1", ",", "0"}], "]"}], ".", 
          RowBox[{"op", "[", 
           RowBox[{"q2", ",", "t"}], "]"}], ".", 
          RowBox[{"op", "[", 
           RowBox[{"q1", ",", "0"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"q1", ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"q2", ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
    "]"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9860459868068104`*^9, 3.9860460294940376`*^9}, {
   3.986046102155222*^9, 3.986046107648388*^9}, {3.9860499408524094`*^9, 
   3.986049988291706*^9}, {3.986050019235214*^9, 3.9860500234739494`*^9}, {
   3.9860635883968887`*^9, 3.9860636020671844`*^9}, {3.986066136054428*^9, 
   3.9860661901803856`*^9}, {3.9860673225903263`*^9, 3.986067338303793*^9}, {
   3.986474312776371*^9, 3.986474330653557*^9}, {3.99840440593824*^9, 
   3.998404427415863*^9}, {3.998405077447708*^9, 3.9984050891254463`*^9}, {
   3.9984051636978226`*^9, 3.998405164482338*^9}, {3.998405216475607*^9, 
   3.99840522517222*^9}, {3.9984053384569645`*^9, 3.9984053385692425`*^9}, 
   3.9984055762200356`*^9, {3.998405749079464*^9, 3.998405749825016*^9}, {
   3.9984282338633785`*^9, 3.998428253904312*^9}, {3.9984284256105156`*^9, 
   3.998428426340334*^9}, {3.998428524564348*^9, 3.9984286996542473`*^9}, {
   3.998429355135908*^9, 3.9984295091259823`*^9}, {3.9984296025484676`*^9, 
   3.998429604663557*^9}, {3.9984296888735046`*^9, 3.9984297024157352`*^9}, {
   3.998432889326372*^9, 3.998432890821844*^9}, 3.9985793409467907`*^9, 
   3.9985895225366783`*^9, {3.9986545247209435`*^9, 3.9986545372278633`*^9}, {
   3.998654849807665*^9, 3.9986548956952896`*^9}, {3.998654994125391*^9, 
